Z||000062||PK||12-20-2001||07:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B> I've got that exact bottle of Edradour... yummy.  Visited the distillery outside of Pitlochery.  The Edradour is one of the parts to both the House of Lords and the King's Ransom blends. I'll gladly take either   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If you happen to come across a bottle of King's Ransom, I'll pay quite nicely for it.  I've only managed to find 1 bottle of it here in the states- and it's in California... and is listed to sell for over $150 for a bottle!  I want it!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>MinnGreen, there's a bottle of "House of Lords" sat next to me with your name on. All I need is a delivery address!!  King's Ransom is no longer available even directly from the distillers! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> <P>Cheers<BR>PK<P>||||reg||10
Z||000063||WampusCat||12-20-2001||09:39 AM||||It's funny whenever I've been to Mexico, all the locals are drinking Budweiser and the U.S. tourists are drinking Corona.  My favorite U.S. beer that is nationally available is Sierra Nevada Ale followed by Sam Adams.  Yeungling makes a great porter if you like dark beers.  Bosco's is the beer I drink most, but it's only in TN.  Here's one from Pontiac, MI, birthplace of the Fiero:  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/b_amber2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by WampusCat (edited 12-20-2001).]||||reg||1
