Z||000067||Formula88||12-21-2001||11:14 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>I'm a wine guy, but I'll toss in another 5 votes for Guiness.  Anything with a 'widget' inside has just got to be cool.<P>Yeah.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>PS: I vote six times for a good 10 year old cabernet!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, especially the new Bottled Guiness Draft with the New and Improved <B><I>ROCKET WIDGET!</B></I>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Speaking of Cab (well, red wine), have you tried Ravenswood Zinfindel?  To be a Zin, it's incredibly smooth.  It's my "standard" wine.  If I'm looking for something a bit nicer, Blackstone, Firestone, or Chateau Ste. Michelle is good.  Iron Horse Merlot... ah, the list is too long.  <P>Bouchane Pinot Noir, yummy!<P>Oh, I know where you can get a lovely '45 Mouton Rothschilde, if you're interested.  <P>A wine's first job is to be <FONT COLOR="red"><B>red</B></FONT>.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 12-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000068||Tina||12-21-2001||05:18 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Butter:<BR><B>I've tried most of the beers yall have mentioned so far but my vote goes for<BR>COLD BEER</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ahhhh, but such a relative term   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Do you mean <BR><B>Cold</B> as in, it's been sitting on the garage floor since you brought it home from the store,and the distance to and from the house is too far to warrant putting it into the fridge while working in the garage.<BR>  <BR><B>Cold</B> as in, came right out of the fridge, but then...<BR>What shelf was it sitting on?<BR>Topshelf or the one with veggie setting?<P><B>Cold</B> as in, out of a cooler full ice it'd been sitting in for quit a while.<BR>Dripping cold icy water......I could go on  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><B>Cold</B> as in, stored in the freezer for just the right time and turns into a beer slushy as soon as you open it.<P><BR>(We won't talk about the ones somebody forgot to take out of the freezer in time)<P>Tina   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 12-21-2001).]||||reg||1
